{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1209124-post-limit-break","id":1209124,"title":"Post limit break","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2018-04-19T23:00:00-07:00","id":1209124,"title":"Post limit break","content":"Hey Everyone.<br /> <br /> I have a question regarding limit and the limit break. <br /> <br /> It says in the book that experiencing limitbreak is a good feeling, like a release of all that pent up energy. Now I wonder if this is only the case if you actually get to live out your limit break.<br /> <br /> I ask this because my Solar Silver Wisp had her first limit last time my group played, the session revolved around the attack on a double dealing necromancer in our city. To put it mildly, it was poorly planned. Most of the group was divided and attacked from various directions and we had no idea what to expect (Except for Necromancer stuff) My characters limit broke just in the beginning of the battle and my GM and I had previously found the nice virtueflaw from compassion called Smothering Overprotection where my character becomes consumed with a desire to protect her friends. <br /> <br /> So the problem was that no matter how she tried they all ended up getting injured (some quite quite bad) so she didnt actually protect anything she just ran from place to place and was late every time. To make matters worse she broke out of her limit early as she ended up hurting one of the others and giving him some really horrible wounds because of it. <br /> <br /> Now taking the above into consideration I cannot see how my character would look back on the experience and think it was a good or just a necessary thing. But what are your thoughts?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13663-adaras","name":"Adaras","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13663_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"14"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-19T23:14:15-07:00","id":1209126,"title":"","content":"I've always viewed the idea that limit feels good being either an expression of catharsis or just a release of stress and complication. Now I believe they got rid of that particular phrasing in 3rd, but in 2nd I think the actual description on the willpower refresh required you to fully ride out the limit break, so that specifically wouldn't fit the feel better scenario if I'm remembering it right.<br /> <br /> Now how your character would spin this into a positive experience, well she knows what she needs to do now. Every time she tried to save one of her friends she was late, if they'd been in more danger they'd be dead. Beyond even that she fracked up and hurt one of them, so she's probably justified in having this be the wake up call on needing to focus and get better to be able to protect her friends so she won't fail again. The experience itself not being positive, but the assurance of purpose and clear direction would make her feel better and potentially lead to the whole thing being viewed in a more positive light long term.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3400-nalak42","name":"nalak42","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3400_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2931"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-19T23:23:41-07:00","id":1209127,"title":"","content":"Hey Nalak42 <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> Thanks for the quick response. <br /> <br /> &quot;Being in Limit Break is an intensely emotional experience,<br /> a powerful cathartic reaction to whatever stress<br /> has driven a character to it\u2014it feels good, or at least necessary,<br /> even as it is traumatic.&quot; This is from the 3rd edition pdf I have (Dont have my book with me sadly)<br /> <br /> I like your idea on how she can make it a learning experience for herself <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> The only problem is that she is really self-doubting (One of her defining is that she dosnt think she is good enough or worthy of being an exalt) + now she fears that when the others find out that she hurt on of the others she fears that they hate her. So she did kinda flee after she got out of her limit break, the battle was over luckily.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13663-adaras","name":"Adaras","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13663_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"14"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-20T01:58:09-07:00","id":1209153,"title":"","content":"In this particular case, I would prioritize the bit about it feeling <i>necessary</i> over it feeling <i>good</i>.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-20T05:06:04-07:00","id":1209182,"title":"","content":"Catharsis is more about relief, clarity, than &quot;feeling nice&quot;. Try going with that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse/visitormessage/1408635-visitor-message-from-synapse#post1408635\" target=\"_blank\">Check my Exalted homebrew</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse","name":"Synapse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar32_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1507"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-20T09:14:03-07:00","id":1209281,"title":"","content":"I could see the character feeling sorrow over the way things turned out, but relief over having actually tried rather than just sitting around frustrated. She can see now how things went wrong but having acted and knowing how to do better next time granting a... clarity of purpose I guess would be a good way of saying it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4862-sequal","name":"Sequal","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4862_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"46"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-20T10:31:27-07:00","id":1209313,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Adaras</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1209124-post-limit-break?p=1209127#post1209127\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hey Nalak42 <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> Thanks for the quick response.<br /> <br /> &quot;Being in Limit Break is an intensely emotional experience,<br /> a powerful cathartic reaction to whatever stress<br /> has driven a character to it\u2014it feels good, or at least necessary,<br /> even as it is traumatic.&quot; This is from the 3rd edition pdf I have (Dont have my book with me sadly)<br /> <br /> I like your idea on how she can make it a learning experience for herself <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> The only problem is that she is really self-doubting (One of her defining is that she dosnt think she is good enough or worthy of being an exalt) + now she fears that when the others find out that she hurt on of the others she fears that they hate her. So she did kinda flee after she got out of her limit break, the battle was over luckily.</div> </div> </div> </div>Fair, I didn't do too thorough a read through on the limit break when I was checking since it wasn't high priority for the response. <br /> <br /> Now as for going forward, well she thinks she's a screw up who shouldn't have this power. Seems like an excellent drive to seek power, connections, a mentor, virtually anything to enable her to rectify the mistake and be able to avoid what she believes is the inevitable response.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3400-nalak42","name":"nalak42","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3400_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2931"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}